From f2fa35baeb0bbbdaa71a6060d7831b4c1c818620 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:47:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: survive a yanked or unmounted recording drive

A drive pulled or unmounted during a take used to end the take by accident:
the first failed write latched a generic "Input/output error", the stop path
then reopened, renamed and fsynced files on the dead mount, lossy DNG takes
never stopped at all (the background writer only logged), the queued frames
vanished uncounted, and the UIs learned nothing until the 1 s poll showed
"recording_error". Nothing gated record_start on media, so a take with no
drive landed on the SD card.

Logic ported from Cinemate's storage handling, in Core's own shape:

- util/MediaFault.hpp: errno -> {Removed, Full, ReadOnly, Permission, Other}
  (Cinemate's yank set EIO/ENOENT/ENODEV/ENOTCONN/ESTALE plus ENXIO), one
  operator message per class, a machine name for state fields.
- util/MediaProbe.hpp: is the media root a mount point (/proc/mounts, exact
  path match, last entry wins) and does statvfs on the mount root answer; the
  decision is a pure function, host-tested.
- ApertarCoreApp: a media watcher thread (1 s idle, 250 ms while recording)
  that holds no shared lock while it probes, publishes a broadcast "media"
  event on every change, flags the controller when a mounted medium is lost
  mid-take and ends the take through the existing supervisor path; state
  fields media_state/media_alive/media_device/media_fstype/recording_fault in
  /api/state and get_state; one record gate in handleCommand (mounted, alive,
  >= APERTAR_MEDIA_MIN_FREE_MB free; APERTAR_MEDIA_REQUIRE_MOUNT=0 for dev
  machines) covering socket, WebUI and buttons.
- DngRecordingQueue: catch sites classify the errno (std::system_error) and
  latch the class; frames discarded at the latch and frames offered after it
  are counted (discarded_on_failure=, skipped_after_failure=, fault= in the
  stats line); lossy DNG background-write failures now surface one frame late
  and end the take; stop(mediumDead) skips the lossy drain and the MLV header
  patch (MlvEncoder::abandon).
- CameraSession::stopRecording(mediumGone): H.264 leaves its .mp4.writing in
  place, audio does not finalise the WAV or reopen the raw capture, nothing
  touches the medium again.
- MlvEncoder keeps the errno behind its text errors; LossyDngDiskWriter
  counts failures and can abandon its queue.
- Eject intent: util/MediaIntent.hpp writes /run/apertar-media/eject/<dev>
  before a deliberate unmount and clears it on remount or when the device
  node is gone, for an automounter to honour (Cinemate f01b6cd).
- WebUI: record button disabled without media, "MEDIA REMOVED" status.

Host-checked: MlvEncoder.cpp, LossyDngEncoder.cpp, AudioRecordingSession.cpp,
ApertarCoreApp.cpp and WebControlPage.cpp pass g++ -fsyntax-only; the new
headers pass tools/media_probe_test (KB). CameraController.cpp needs libcamera
and is not compiled here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
